<!-- 7 ▸ BELIEF 3 · THE MECHANISM (one section, one chart) -->
<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>The wheat bag goes cold. This holds.</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <figure class="fig split-media">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 380 240" role="img" aria-label="Chart comparing temperature over a 30 minute session: a wheat bag drops from hot to room temperature within about 10 minutes, while Jointwell holds its set heat for the full session.">
          <line x1="46" y1="20" x2="46" y2="196" stroke="#e6e0d8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <line x1="46" y1="196" x2="366" y2="196" stroke="#e6e0d8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <g font-family="system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#8a8177">
            <text x="8" y="46">{{ t_max }}°C</text>
            <text x="8" y="192">Cool</text>
            <text x="46" y="214">0 min</text>
            <text x="180" y="214">15 min</text>
            <text x="330" y="214">30 min</text>
          </g>
          <path d="M46 42 C 90 60, 120 150, 170 178 L 366 186" fill="none" stroke="#b9b0a4" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="6 5"/>
          <path d="M46 42 L 366 42" fill="none" stroke="#c8500f" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          <g font-family="Archivo,sans-serif" font-weight="700" font-size="12">
            <text x="215" y="34" fill="#c8500f">Jointwell holds its set heat</text>
            <text x="150" y="168" fill="#8a8177">Wheat bag</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>An illustration of session warmth. A wheat bag runs hottest at the start and fades from there, with roughly 30 minutes of useful heat in it. Jointwell holds whichever level you set, {{ t_min }}°C to {{ t_max }}°C, until the 30 minutes are up.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);margin-bottom:14px">A hot water bottle holds its warmth for twenty minutes or so. A microwaved wheat bag, about the same. Guidance says apply heat for fifteen to twenty minutes, so the thing in your cupboard delivers roughly the right dose and then dies, and asks you to sit still for all of it.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);margin-bottom:14px">Jointwell holds the level you set for the full thirty minutes, between {{ t_min }}°C and {{ t_max }}°C, with vibration massage running alongside it at one of three strengths.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-soft)">It is cordless and 360&nbsp;g, so it straps on and runs itself. On with the first cup of tea, still on while the kettle goes. Most people put it on with the first cup of tea.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

